#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
modelm-remap — remap keys on an IBM Model M connected through a Soarer's Converter.

It talks to the converter directly:
  1. listens for the key you physically press,
  2. shows a menu of target keys (Command / Option / etc. first),
  3. rewrites the converter's EEPROM config so the remap survives reboots.

The low-level tools (scas / scdis / sctool) are vendored under ./vendor/bin and
built by ./build.sh. Nothing is compiled on the fly and no daemon is installed.

Examples
  modelm-remap                     interactive wizard (press a key -> choose target)
  modelm-remap set RALT LGUI       non-interactive remap
  modelm-remap screenshot           press a key -> Cmd+Shift+4 (region screenshot)
  modelm-remap copy                 press a key -> Cmd+C
  modelm-remap paste                press a key -> Cmd+V
  modelm-remap select-all           press a key -> Cmd+A
  modelm-remap macro               press a key -> choose a shortcut to send
  modelm-remap shortcut F10 CMD+SHIFT+4   non-interactive shortcut macro
  modelm-remap listen              print keys as you press them
  modelm-remap show                show the config currently in the converter
  modelm-remap keys                list all valid key names
  modelm-remap info                firmware / EEPROM info
"""

